{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "08-trigger-bindings",
  "title": "Trigger bindings",
  "description": "How a trigger binding starts a workflow and where the run happens. Left: the four RUN_TRIGGER kinds converge on the binding's `trigger kind` field; under them, the pr-label label state machine (agent:review → agent:in-progress → agent:blocked, all GitHub Actions labels). Center: the Binding record (outside the workflow YAML) with its five fields. Right: the `run location` field goes straight to local (version 1) in Run locations, or, in Piece 2 (above), to the Scheduler on services-01, which picks dev-01 or sandbox by load. Key: green solid = version 1; violet dashed = later / reserved.",
  "mode": "diagram",
